---
/**
 * Decorative figure for the home hero, filling the half of the band the text
 * leaves empty.
 *
 * Inline, and that is the point rather than a convenience. An SVG referenced
 * through <img src> is a separate document that no stylesheet of ours reaches:
 * no `currentColor`, no token, nothing that follows the theme. Inlined, it
 * costs no extra request, it gzips with the HTML, and its accent switches with
 * the palette. A raster would need two files and a media query to do as much.
 *
 * It is the brand mark itself, large, cropped by the band, with one of its four
 * strokes carrying the accent. Three discarded attempts are the reason for that
 * rather than a preference:
 *
 *   - Horizontal rules crossed by a diagonal, meant to read as lines of text,
 *     read as two other things instead. The diagonal with a node on it became a
 *     growth chart, and pale evenly spaced rules became a skeleton loading
 *     state, which is the last thing to evoke on a blog that argues about page
 *     weight.
 *   - The mark at 60% of the band with a wide bleed stopped being a mark: it
 *     read as unrelated grey petals beside a coloured wedge.
 *   - The accent on a diagonal outweighed the title's second line, which is the
 *     wrong order, and on the upper diagonal the band's edge sliced the colour
 *     mid-stroke, which reads as a mistake and not as a crop.
 *
 * So the accent sits on the upper lobe: a slim crescent, whole, at the far side
 * from the text. Moving it back to a diagonal is moving one class.
 *
 * Weight is why this is hand-written rather than exported from a drawing tool.
 * The three Docusaurus illustrations still in public/img weigh 128.5, 52.8 and
 * 37.1 kB, and svgo recovers only 15.6% because the weight sits in the path
 * data. These four paths are the ones the logo already ships, and the whole
 * figure costs 0.4 kB gzipped in the page.
 *
 * Purely decorative, so `aria-hidden`: everything it means, the title says in
 * words.
 */
---

<svg
  class="figure"
  viewBox="0 0 451.17 454.85"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  {/* The three quiet strokes, in the page's own ink at low opacity, so the mark
      reads as a watermark and never competes with the title. */}
  <g class="figure__quiet">
    <path
      d="m302.16,316.77c-76.98,1.24-140.96,50.21-163.47,121.28,26.49,10.8,55.44,16.8,85.8,16.8,93.98,0,174.63-57.01,209.29-138.33-43.88-.18-87.76-.46-131.62.25"
    />
    <path
      d="m6.12,251.54c-2.24,4.03-4.24,8.14-6.12,12.28,11.17,69.43,53.77,128.31,112.75,161.65,40.07-82.16,79.93-163.88,119.75-245.53-56.89-34.36-172.23-25.87-226.38,71.59"
    />
    <path
      d="m392.21,266.63c25.47-15.7,45.13-34.74,58.96-56.8-5.67-74.07-46.77-138.18-106.44-175.43-38.91,79.79-77.95,159.83-117.46,240.83,57.07,25.19,112.59,23.67,164.94-8.61"
    />
  </g>

  {/* The upper lobe, and the only part of the figure that follows the theme. */}
  <path
    class="figure__accent"
    d="m152.86,138.35c78.19-.88,143.48-49.69,166.39-117.65C290.4,7.44,258.32,0,224.49,0,130.46,0,49.76,57.07,15.13,138.47c45.91.12,91.83.4,137.73-.12"
  />
</svg>

<style>
  .figure {
    /* Large, and cropped by the band on the trailing edge only. The z has to
       stay recognisable, which means most of it has to be inside. */
    inline-size: min(22rem, 38%);
    block-size: auto;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-inline-end: calc(var(--space-12) * -1);
  }

  .figure__quiet path {
    fill: var(--color-text);
    opacity: 0.07;
  }

  .figure__accent {
    /* Full strength, no opacity. Half-transparent, the light theme's blue came
       out lavender, a colour the brand does not have: a tinted accent is worse
       than no accent. Scale is what keeps it from shouting over the title. */
    fill: var(--color-primary);
  }

  /* Below the breakpoint where the hero stacks, the figure would push the
     actions off the first screen for nothing: it says nothing the title does
     not. Hidden rather than shrunk. It still ships, being inline, but 0.4 kB is
     a fair price for one rule instead of a second asset. */
  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .figure {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
